From 0b21c238d509de2716fb57edc6ae5cdc15a0cc58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HampterDev <131729366+HampterDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:51:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Go on without the reputation, item-name, item-reform and
 enchant managers when they cannot be allocated

The same as 91ba2d9 for the four other managers that app_init_managers
loads through an instance function allocating on first use:
repute_mgr_load, item_db_to_id_load, item_reform_mgr_load and
enchant_mgr_load got NULL when mem_try_alloc failed and reached the
manager's Lua script or tables through it. The loads are skipped now,
and startup goes on as when they fail (their results were not looked
at).

The 29 later users ask the instance again and get NULL while memory is
short. Each now gets the answer of a manager whose file did not load:
- reputation (repute_wnd.c, repute_wnd_pages.c, game/repute.c): the
  group, info and search lists are empty, set_points stores nothing,
  set_info_result still refreshes the window and on_changed still opens
  it with the general "changed" text, and the window's draw shows the
  "no information" notice for a missing manager, as for no_info;
- item names (enchant_mgr.c, item_reform.c): item_db_to_id_lookup
  already answered 0 for a NULL manager;
- item reform (item_reform_list.c, item_reform_wnd.c,
  mode_item_reform.c): no base items, no reform found, no reform item,
  and the window's material slots come from the new
  item_reform_max_materials, REFORM_MAX_MATERIALS (6) without a
  manager, which is what an unloaded manager holds;
- enchants (enchant_wnd.c, and the 12 Lua callbacks of enchant_lua.c):
  enchant_mgr_find_list finds no list, so the window closes as for an
  unknown table, and the setters store nothing.

test_manager_alloc_failure now covers the six managers: the startup
loads extracted from app_init_managers, the four managers' files linked
whole with their outside calls stubbed (tests/
manager_alloc_failure_stubs.c, where a Lua script reached through a
NULL manager stops the test), and every user check run twice, without
memory and on new managers that have not loaded, with the same
answers. It fails on the previous code with startup.c reverted
("repute_mgr_load was called with NULL"), with repute_mgr.c or
enchant_mgr.c reverted (an access violation), with item_reform.c
reverted (it has no item_reform_max_materials; with only that function
added, an access violation in the lookups).

